<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- March 21-23.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- March 21-23.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the March 21-23 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Liar Liar		  $31,423,025	 $  ----</p>
<p>2. Selena		     $11,615,722	 $  ----</p>
<p>3. Return of the Jedi     $ 7,517,738	 $ 27,501,267</p>
<p>4. Jungle 2 Jungle	  $ 6,016,059	 $ 35,591,374</p>
<p>5. Private Parts	    $ 4,403,410	 $ 34,448,633</p>
<p>6. Donnie Brasco	    $ 3,316,087	 $ 36,259,575</p>
<p>7. Sling Blade		$ 3,017,085	 $ 12,524,591</p>
<p>8. Love Jones		 $ 2,551,763	 $  7,511,075</p>
<p>9. The Empire</p>
<p>    Strikes Back	    $ 2,427,835	 $ 63,356,239</p>
<p>10 The English Patient    $ 2,015,118	 $ 63,154,818</p>
<p>NOTE: Lifetime domestic gross for &quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot; is $286,030,505 and &quot;Return of the Jedi&quot; is $291,235,909.</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Selena&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.. &quot;Love Jones&quot; is released by Time Warner's New Line Cinema.</p>
<p>&quot;Return of the Jedi&quot; and &quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Jungle 2 Jungle&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co. while &quot;Sling Blade&quot; and &quot;The English Patient&quot; are released by Disney's Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;Private Parts&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Donnie Brasco&quot; is released by Sony Corp..</p>
</text>
